{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"8a72bf6e-222c-4e60-94fb-b9a666aef228","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have successfully completed the `lab-14-global-memory` project according to your instructions. \n\nHere is a summary of the actions taken:\n1. **Created Simulator (`gms_sim.c`)**: Wrote a C11 program that simulates an N-node cluster caching system, calculating `MinAge` and selecting a target node based on weights for global replacement. It also benchmarks memory fetch times locally (`memcpy`) versus remotely (simulated via UNIX `socketpair`). \n2. **Created Makefile**: Provided `all`, `run`, `test`, and `clean` commands.\n3. **VM testing \u0026 `expected-output.txt`**: Successfully executed `run-in-vm.sh lab-14-global-memory test` inside the nested KVM and captured the test output (`~10x` slower for remote socket fetch compared to local).\n4. **Updated `README.md`**: Completed the seed document with prerequisites, execution steps, captured logs, 3 experiments, and 3 folded QA blocks with `status: solid`.\n5. **Git commit**: Cleanly staged the 5 files (including `.gitignore`) and committed with a conventional format on `aos/writer-part-0-1`.\n6. **Generated Report**: The summary report has been saved directly to `/Users/shreejitverma/github/career-ops/library/01-CS-Foundations/Operating-Systems/CS6210-AOS/crew/runner/reports/lab-14-global-memory.md`.\n\nNo human intervention was required, and the honor code requirements were strictly maintained by focusing exclusively on a simulator.\n","duration_seconds":188.62889,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":128222,"output_tokens":15175,"thinking_tokens":8104,"cache_read_tokens":936416,"total_tokens":143397}}}
